(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[8 1 "// Descriptors (PY5c; CPython's Objects/descrobject.c, funcobject.c's classmethod and staticmethod,"] [9 1 "// classobject.c's method, typeobject.c's super and slot wrappers): bound methods, functions as"] [10 1 "// descriptors, classmethod, staticmethod, property, __slots__' members, super, the slot wrappers"] [11 1 "// that show a built-in type's slots as methods, and the attributes of types, functions and methods."] [24 1 "// Method is a bound method: a function and the object it is bound to."] [31 1 "// ClassMethod and StaticMethod wrap a callable."] [46 1 "// Property is property(fget, fset, fdel, doc)."] [50 27 "// a subclass of property"] [60 1 "// Member is a __slots__ entry's descriptor."] [69 1 "// Super is super(type, obj)."] [78 1 "// slotWrapper is a built-in type's slot as a method (wrapper_descriptor)."] [87 1 "// mappingProxy is a type's __dict__ read only."] [90 11 "// the type whose __dict__ it is, or nil"] [91 11 "// the mapping, when it is no dict (mappingproxy(UserDict()))"] [94 1 "// proxied is the mapping behind p."] [118 1 "// newWrappers are the built-in types' __new__ objects, one each."] [126 1 "// slotWrappers keep one wrapper per type and name, so that int.__repr__ is int.__repr__ (enum compares"] [127 1 "// a class's methods with its data type's and object's; PY5e, part 2b)."] [130 1 "// slotWrapperFor is built-in type m's slot for the special method name, or nil."] [157 2 "// the number protocol's binary methods (__add__, __radd__, __iadd__ ...): the Binary, RBinary and InPlace"] [158 2 "// slots, NotImplemented when they do not apply (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200: test_asyncio reads int.__add__)"] [183 6 "// wrap_ternaryfunc_r: the operands swapped, the modulus third"] [202 4 "// object_str: tp_repr, never the type's own __str__ (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: a class with"] [203 4 "// __str__ = object.__str__, doctest's DocTestCase, recursed without end)"] [324 5 "// dict_subscript sees self's type: a subclass's d.__getitem__(k) calls its __missing__ as d[k] does"] [325 5 "// (queue 202: urllib.parse's _Quoter(safe).__getitem__ raised KeyError: test_http_cookies,"] [326 5 "// test_wsgiref's request_uri)"] [434 3 "// one object per type, so that object.__new__ is object.__new__ (enum's _find_new_ compares them;"] [435 3 "// PY5e, part 2b)"] [518 1 "// hackCheck is hackcheck: m's __setattr__ called on self, whose built-in base nearest to its type overrides it"] [519 1 "// (object.__setattr__(str, ...) would jump over type's own)."] [536 1 "// objectDir is object.__dir__: the instance's dictionary's keys and its class's attributes."] [597 1 "// superArgs are super()'s zero arguments: the running function's first argument and its __class__ cell."] [635 2 "// supercheck: a proxy's __class__ (a class it pretends to be an instance of)"] [665 2 "// functions as descriptors, bound methods"] [672 2 "// types.MethodType(func, instance) (method_new)"] [698 2 "// method_descr_get: a bound method is not bound again (gh-113157)"] [737 2 "// slot wrappers"] [768 2 "// classmethod, staticmethod (funcobject.c): a subclass's instance is an Instance around the Go value, so every"] [769 2 "// slot unwraps; __init__ copies the wrapped callable's attributes (functools_wraps) into the dict"] [872 3 "// descriptor_get_wrapped_attribute and its setter: the dict first, the callable's value kept there"] [917 2 "// property"] [1049 2 "// __slots__' members"] [1130 2 "// super"] [1177 5 "// a built-in type's method, or a method descriptor in a heap type's dict (methodDescrs: _ast's AST,"] [1178 5 "// queue 202c: super().__init__ in a node class's subclass)"] [1206 53 "// a subclass of super: its type called"] [1228 2 "// mappingproxy"] [1230 2 "// mappingproxy(mapping), over a dict (PY6a: enum's __members__); other mappings are the data model's"] [1241 3 "// mappingproxy_check_mapping: PyMapping_Check, not a list or a tuple"] [1251 2 "// a built-in type's own slots' wrappers (ownSlots, registry.go) are in its __dict__ too (PY5e, part 2b)"] [1259 14 "// a built-in type's attribute descriptors (type.__dict__['__annotations__']: annotationlib)"] [1291 2 "// mappingproxy_richcompare: the mapping's own comparison (queue 202: mappingproxy({}) == {} was False; test_re's"] [1292 2 "// test_getattr compares a pattern's groupindex with a dict)"] [1317 2 "// mappingproxy_or: the mappings beneath, a proxy's unwrapped on either side"] [1440 21 "// inside the first mro()"] [1494 33 "// type_mro: mro_implementation afresh, a metaclass's mro() builds on it"] [1545 1 "// checkSetSpecial is check_set_special_type_attr."] [1727 2 "// __module__ is func.go's (PY6d's R5: the function's module), which this init's order let override this one"] [1730 1 "// excSlots are the __slots__ values of exceptions (an exception class's instances are *Exception, not"] [1731 1 "// *Instance): PY6a, by the integration's owner, for test_exceptions' slotted exception classes."] [1734 1 "// setTypeBases is type.__bases__'s setter (typeobject.c's type_set_bases; PY6b's request: typing.NamedTuple"] [1735 1 "// assigns a class's bases): a heap type's bases replaced by types of the same instance layout, its MRO and its"] [1736 1 "// subclasses' computed again and their slots refilled."] [1755 3 "// a reentrant mro() has not set base's MRO yet: its __base__ is asked too"] [1781 2 "// nothing more when a reentrant assignment replaced the bases"] [1800 1 "// newStaticBase is tp_new_wrapper's staticbase (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's test_bad_new): t, or"] [1801 1 "// the first base along __base__ whose __new__ is not a Python class's own (slot_tp_new)."] [1809 1 "// newOrigin is the built-in type whose __new__ t's tp_new is (inherited along __base__ from the first one"] [1810 1 "// that defines it), CPython's tp_new pointer compared."] [1824 1 "// newAliases: the built-in types whose own __new__ here is CPython's inherited one (defaultdict's is dict_new)"] [1827 1 "// isNewWrapper: v is a built-in type's __new__ (tp_new_wrapper); a class whose __new__ is one keeps the"] [1828 1 "// __new__ it inherits (update_one_slot's special case), so that class C(list): __new__ = object.__new__"] [1829 1 "// makes lists"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[133 29] [151 37] [191 37] [204 67] [215 63] [220 68] [225 67] [241 37] [258 37] [280 37] [287 38] [319 37] [323 25] [337 38] [342 37] [352 37] [375 37] [413 38] [418 37] [436 26] [450 29] [477 25] [479 38] [497 37] [522 12] [522 22] [543 24] [545 24] [568 24] [629 26] [640 24] [647 23] [690 34] [693 36] [703 54] [705 57] [728 55] [742 27] [780 26] [787 41] [800 40] [835 22] [855 27] [877 24] [948 38] [956 28] [958 56] [998 42] [1024 50] [1034 53] [1039 48] [1040 26] [1051 26] [1058 31] [1059 32] [1068 22] [1074 26] [1078 31] [1105 26] [1112 26] [1118 26] [1124 26] [1133 43] [1172 51] [1179 29] [1185 36] [1216 29] [1222 29] [1235 38] [1238 30] [1257 23] [1258 36] [1274 25] [1286 31] [1319 32] [1359 47] [1375 51] [1388 39] [1396 48] [1399 23] [1411 34] [1417 45] [1432 25] [1451 43] [1461 47] [1475 26] [1485 25] [1578 22] [1582 46] [1584 25] [1588 49] [1590 27] [1607 29] [1624 29] [1652 29] [1665 27] [1702 23] [1713 30] [1721 28] [1739 46] [1765 62] [1771 34] [1772 25] [1772 33] [1812 23] [1835 34]]} (go/file "descr.go" :imports [


